<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="BlueMonk-Bb-Theme" spTempo="120">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1954
Composer:	Thelonious Monk
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	12-bar blues
Style:	Bebop-influenced jazz blues swing
Key:	Bb major

“Blue Monk” was composed and first recorded by Thelonious
Monk in 1954 for Thelonious Monk Trio. It is one of Monk’s most
accessible blues themes, built around a memorable chromatic
motif and a traditional dominant-blues progression; Abbey Lincoln
later added lyrics and called her version “Monkery’s the Blues.” </spComments>
